+The 2026-11-05 addendum to the 19:34 report already stated that the installation
+demand was superseded. The 2026-11-22 retro-addendum then said “Nothing in the
+original report's substantive claims is superseded,” while also saying no
+deployment was required. That broad sentence is inaccurate as applied to the
+host-installation demand and is clarified here: the demand is superseded; the
+withdrawal controls. The 2026-11-22 addendum's caution that its 2 November
+byte-identity observation is historical and not a current verification remains
+valid.
+
+## Evidence and scope
+
+I read the current Founder instruction in this dispatch, the exact historical
+reports/dispositions identified above, `20261102T183925Z-founder-charter-deployment-blocked.judiciary-addendum-2026-11-03.md`,
+`20261102T193457Z-founder-constitution-correction.judiciary-addendum-2026-11-05.md`,
+and `20261102T193457Z-founder-constitution-correction.judicia-retro-addendum-20261122.md`.
+Together they establish withdrawal, the prior unsupported installation demand,
+and the earlier correction. I did not inspect or modify the Founder-controlled
+constitutional mount; no such inspection is needed to determine whether the
+withdrawn proposal may be deployed. This is a correction of judicial reporting,
+not a constitutional change or a new deployment instruction.
+
+Original reports and dispositions remain unchanged. No law, measurement system,
+or case state was changed; no reform is proposed.
