+# Independent Judiciary evidence report — cycle `ee037ddab870918de8a4fe9d9508ad68`
+
+Date: 2026-11-25. Audience: Legislature and Founder. Acts 4, 8, 9, 12.11 and 15.
+Fact-finding and measurement only; no law, correction trail, audit machinery,
+case state, activation, or productive ownership was changed.
+
+## Method and cohort
+
+Read `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/oversight/audit-evidence.txt`, the frozen
+selection `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/oversight/audit-selection-ee037ddab870918de8a4fe9d9508ad68.json`,
+current `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche/government/LAWS.md` and `OVERSIGHT.md`, current
+live Antonina records, canonical Git and local state. The frozen cohort has four
+cases: two open issues, one claimed delivery and one government decision. Each
+received a first-filing `audit-accountability.py report` verdict; no correction
+was filed, so no correction command (or cycle token) was used. Case verdicts are
+auditable assertions, not machine proofs. The predecessor's separate cycle
+`9318b6071c88df33ea64fb1093e847c5` reports are not substituted for this new
+frozen cohort.
+
+The pending Judiciary mailbox directory was empty at inspection. The dispatch
+lists `open_cases: []`; no case-state change was made. The prior
+`continuity_unverified_judiciary` case is already `verified_closed`, so I did not
+write a duplicate continuity receipt. I inspected its older terminal event,
+status, log tail, saved worktree head/status, and its reconciliation receipt.
+The receipt's previous/successor IDs exactly match the existing
+`continuity/verified-judiciary.json`; commits `a9c8a18`, `5b8db8c` and `753468c`
+are ancestors of canonical `origin/main`, confirming the specific addendum,
+delivery and resource-report effects. Limitation: the old terminal snapshot
+records a very dirty worktree, its captured `753468c` head is not the current
+branch head, and Antonina now returns “unknown agent” for the recorded successor
+ID. I therefore rely only on the named landed Git/board effects, not on that
+old readiness assertion or a claim of current successor liveness; I did not
+rewrite the pre-existing verified record.
+
+## Sampled verdicts
+
+1. `e780850d83c2abf4a6`, open `q5I2D47lOkc1Ng85vkZ3AV-frame`, Act 32 Statistics
+   trial — **inconclusive**. The live issue explicitly says `Execution-Host:
+   billy-dev`, establishing assignment. Its latest Executive updates instead
+   report Act 34 HOLD: the four-office measured envelope and prerequisite
+   evidence were insufficient, and `activation.json` remained all-disabled.
+   Act 34 supersedes the proposed earlier Act 32 serial path. This is evidence
+   against an authorized trial being ready, not evidence of neglect or useful
+   delivery. I did not independently re-run the Act 34 gate or check every
+   current permit byte; no activation is claimed.
+2. `8351cdcea1d19e43a3`, open `JMCkOBUsChiTrgkuFnvKLF-looking`, Ivanka P2 —
+   **finding (host/scope only)**. The description directs external Ivanka work
+   and gives no `Execution-Host: billy-dev` assignment or exact-author Founder
+   assignment. Recent scheduler and agent handoffs document Viche-managed work
+   on `marceline-dev`, including the read-only P2 baseline, verification and
+   integration branch. Under current Act 9 / Founder host policy that is a
+   scope/host conflict; it is **not** a neglect finding and is not a finding
+   that the reported calculations or tests are false. The branch's exact head
+   and source hashes are reported in the board thread, but I did not access the
+   external Ivanka clone or independently reproduce its result. GitHub-hosted
+   CI is allowed and is not the basis of this finding.
+3. `fff3dfbb31e21c7cda`, closed imported issue `42` / `skrynia-apps#220` —
+   **inconclusive**. The Antonina history documents the schema, Founder approval
+   of reserved keys, a release-line integration and later reconciliation, but
+   anonymous `git ls-remote https://github.com/ottojung/skrynia-apps.git`
+   failed because credentials were required. I therefore cannot independently
+   confirm the claimed remote merge/release artifact or its current state.
+   This is absence of accessible corroboration, not proof of false delivery.
+4. `fd1c62e486b9f3ae07`, government decision commit
+   `0f26592d3bcdc955b104233e645c8e268f8dee8a`, work-conserving attention —
+   **verified**. Canonical Git confirms the commit is an ancestor of `origin/main`
+   and changes `AGENTS.md`, `government/AGENT-REPORTING-POLICY.md`,
+   `government/executive-agenda.md`, and `missions/pnp/mandate.md`. The specific
+   instruction is present in current policy and directs work-conserving waits,
+   ownership, prompt evidence delivery and no duplicate jobs. This is an
+   operational Founder directive, not a new law; no conflicting ordinary-law
+   change was found in the inspected text. No runtime-effect or agent-uptake
+   claim is made from the commit alone.
+
+## Act 12 review and retrospective correction
+
+The separate reversible Act 12 request `P-1795608432-c579` is independently
+dispositioned in `JUDICIARY-DISPOSITION-2026-11-25-act12-pnp-quarantine-21.md`.
+Primary state/log/ledger checks uphold the exact 21 quarantines and normal grace;
