+The earlier constitutional deployment demand is corrected by
+`JUDICIARY-ADDENDUM-2026-11-25-withdrawn-constitution-deployment-correction.md`;
+the withdrawn amendment is not an open defect and must not be deployed. A
+one-time sample of two generic status dispositions is reviewed in
+`JUDICIARY-ADDENDUM-2026-11-25-generic-disposition-evidence-review.md`; their
+unsupported “verified state” and activity conclusions are explicitly retracted
+as independent verification, not treated as evidence of misconduct.
+
+## Founder outcome measurements and Judiciary operation
+
+- **Quality:** one sampled lawfully recorded operational change was verified at
+  canonical main; one assigned issue is in HOLD with no activation; one open
+  issue has a host/scope finding but its technical work is unverified; and one
+  completed external deliverable remains inaccessible for independent remote
+  confirmation. The sample does not support a blanket quality-success claim.
+- **Timeliness:** the frozen set shows an open HOLD path and an open P2 effort;
+  no issue-specific deadline in the inspected evidence establishes a lateness
+  breach. The September completed-work claim has no current remote check. These
+  are censored observations, not a latency estimate.
+- **Founder attention:** the cohort contains operational directives and a
+  Founder-directed policy commit; no concrete Founder-only decision was raised
+  by this Judiciary review. The PnP review was handled before its deadline.
+  Counts of messages/agents are not treated as attention saved.
+- **Judiciary effectiveness:** all four frozen cases received verdicts, and
+  the PnP action received a separate source-based disposition. This operation
+  did not independently reproduce the Ivanka scientific baseline, authenticate
+  private external GitHub state, or test the live Act 34 runtime. Verdict
+  evidence and these gaps are explicit rather than inferred from agent exits.
+  The post-filing deterministic accountability check at 1795611450 read 528
+  cases, found 0 unreported-overdue samples and individually checked 16 running
+  agent records; it emitted 243 signals: 93 unresolved findings, 124 unresolved
+  inconclusives, 11 ineffective correction-cache claims, 1 pending correction,
+  2 corrected findings and 12 repeated-finding signals. These are collector
+  outputs, not 243 new judicial verdicts; they expose a large unresolved
+  historical queue and the instrument does not distinguish evidence-backed
+  findings from unverified/insufficient-evidence cases in its generic
+  unresolved signal. No signal was hidden or described as a clean result.
+
+## Limitations
+
+Four cases are a small, non-census sample and cannot estimate population-wide
+quality, timeliness or attention. External private-repository access and
+independent host telemetry were unavailable; host evidence rests on board
+content and managed-agent self-reports. Inconclusive means missing positive
+evidence, not misconduct. The deterministic snapshot read for this cycle
+reported 93 findings among 528 cases with 15 running agents checked; a later
+independent re-run of `audit-accountability.py check` confirmed 528 cases,
+93 findings, 0 unreported samples and 243 signals, with 17 running agents
+checked. These are investigative/leading signals only, not delivery counts or a
+verdict, and the running-agent count varies between observations. No reforms are
+proposed by the Judiciary.
